 The entity-specific fields here are the **2021-modified creation guide's minimum inputs**, not an exhaustive later verification checklist. A separate Classic [[raw/adyen/docs/classic-platforms/verification-process/requirements-update/2026-09-15|requirements-update raw]] says its additional rules apply to all new sub-merchants from **1 August 2022** (related raw lines 21–27). It distinguishes EEA owner-or-controller versus non-EEA controller information (related raw lines 43–45) and requires at least one identified signatory with further details (related raw lines 144–146). These two snapshots do not establish that the older minimum payload alone passes later verification checks.
 
+## Related report field discrepancy
+
+The 2019-modified Classic [[source-adyen-docs-classic-platforms-kyc-action-required-snapshot-report|KYC action required snapshot report]] describes its **Entity type** column as only **Business or Individual** ([[raw/adyen/docs/classic-platforms/kyc-action-required-snapshot-report/2026-09-15|report raw line 34]]), while this 2021-modified creation guide lists **Individual, Business, Nonprofit, Partnership and Public company** ([[raw/adyen/docs/classic-platforms/account-holders-and-accounts/2026-09-15|creation raw lines 25–29]]). The two captured pages do not explain how the report represents the additional creation-guide types. Do not infer a mapping or current report behavior from them.
